today's video has been made possible by  one dream an online learning platform  with thousands of courses lectures and  documentaries stick around until the end  to find out more  [Music]  oh  cryptids are undoubtedly some of my  favorite creatures from folklore having  already covered the likes of the mothman  the jersey devil the chupacabra and the  loch ness monster it's about time we  return to north america home to hundreds  of unique and strange creatures  i cannot think of a better place to  start than with bigfoot a creature that  is said to roam the forests of the  united states and canada  bigfoot is also referred to as sasquatch  and the most common description is as a  large hairy ape-like or humanoid  creature that stands anywhere between 6  to 10 feet tall  the name bigfoot originates from a group  of men working for a logging company out  of california in 1958  during several jobs they noticed heavy  equipment and material being moved  around once they established it was none  of them they assumed it must have been  some kind of practical joke a man called  jerry crew came across a set of 16-inch  footprints that he thought were human  the rest of the workers began to see  these footprints and assumed they  belonged to the mysterious prankster  they started calling this mysterious  figure bigfoot  eventually their story as well as a cast  of the footprint would appear in a local  newspaper and thus the legend of bigfoot  began  mentions and depictions of creatures  similar to bigfoot go back centuries and  can be traced back to several native  american tribes those native to what is  now california carved images of wild and  hairy men that are now compared to the  modern idea of bigfoot  most alleged sightings occur in north  west america but spread across the  entirety of north america especially in  rocky and forest dense areas like the  great lakes region  most of these claims are explained as  hoaxes or large animals such as bears  being mistaken for bigfoot those who  claim to have seen bigfoot describe a  range of varying behavior from throwing  rocks and branches at people to hanging  bones of animals on trees to mark his  territory and of course chasing those  pesky trespassers off said territory the  majority of these sightings happen when  it's dark which naturally makes bigfoot  even harder to identify but has also led  to the idea that he is a nocturnal  creature  stories from indigenous tribes speak of  these figures as something to be feared  but also respected they aren't  malevolent or malicious  we do see this with many stories  surrounding bigfoot it's often him  defending his territory  as opposed to going out of his way to  attack someone  despite all the hysteria the hoaxes the  alleged sightings and the skeptics we  are still no closer to finding bigfoot  but one thing is for sure there is no  shortage of people willing to continue  this search  and who knows  maybe one day they'll find what they're  looking for  we find ourselves back in west virginia  this time taking a look at the devil  dogs also known as the white things and  sheepsquatch  most reported sightings of these  creatures happen around the southern  counties of west virginia  their appearance varies from demonic  dogs to something that is more akin to a  yeti or sasquatch that crawls on all  fours commonly they are described as a  creature the size of a bear with white  fur a long pointed head and saber-like  teeth much like the mothman they are  also thought to have come from the tnt  area in mason county those who claim to  have been attacked say it felt as real  as anything they've experienced before  they felt the fangs and claws tearing  into their flesh but when the attack was  over there were no marks  no blood and nothing to suggest they had  even been attacked in the first place  the first reported sighting of the devil  dogs came in 1973  with a family driving by point pleasant  the seven-year-old boy in the back told  his parents he saw something with thick  white shaggy fur that was about three  foot wide  the family then said the creature  appeared right beside the car floating  in the air following them for several  minutes before disappearing  sightings continued over the years along  the roadside but mostly in heavily  wooded areas  the last recorded encounter was in 2015  when six campers came across something  on top of a hill at around at midnight  shining their torches in its direction  they revealed a creature over nine feet  tall that was charging down the hill the  only thing separating them was a small  river the creature stopped around for  several minutes looking for a way to  cross but when it couldn't find one it  jumped in the river and began to swim  across  the group ran back to their campsite  gathered their belongings and fled they  reported the incident to the locals but  not the authorities for fear of not  being believed as it does sound like a  story made up by someone high on shrooms  in the forest  for the next creature we head to maumee  valley in northern indiana where we find  the beast of busco an enormous snapping  turtle  this story begins in 1898 in a small  indiana town known as chirabusco or  busco for short  a farmer named oscar falk came across a  giant turtle living in the lake on his  farm  he told others in the town but no one  would take him seriously and so he  decided against pursuing the turtle any  further  50 years later two locals reported  seeing a turtle that must have weighed  close to 500 pounds whilst they were out  fishing in what was now known as folk  lake the owner of the farm at the time  had also reported seeing the giant  turtle  the story soon became national news and  groups of people flocked to the town in  hopes of seeing this monster turtle for  a town of just over a thousand people  this had a pretty big impact the amount  of people driving to the farm caused so  much traffic the state police were  called in to offer assistance those who  came to see the turtle were extremely  disappointed and questioned whether it  was just a clever ploy by the then owner  gail harris to drive tourism to the town  and his farm  in an effort to clear his name harris  had most of the lake drained but the  turtle now nicknamed the oscar after the  previous owner was nowhere to be seen  several attempts to find him may have  been unsuccessful but the town still  likes to remember oscar as every june  they hold a festival in his memory  a giant turtle in all honesty isn't that  weird but the same can't be said for the  ohio frog man also known as the loveland  frog and the loveland lizard this  cryptid is described as a four foot tall  frog that has been seen all around  loveland ohio the story began in  1955 when a man walking by the roadside  reported seeing three frog-like men with  webbed hands and feet  this could have been easily brushed off  as just another drunk but the reported  sightings continued whilst driving at 3  30 in the morning a man noticed three  reptilian creatures by the road at first  he thought they were humans in costumes  but then he noticed they had leathery  skin like a frog  it gets stranger because one of them  held up what he called a wand and when  sparks began to shoot out he quickly  drove away  could this wand have been a firework  being held by someone in a costume  possibly but i'd like to believe this  man saw three giant frog wizards  practicing magic on the roadside at 3 am  in the morning  interest in the frogmen peaked once  again when the loveland police  themselves killed an animal that matched  its description in 1972 officer ray  shockey was driving when an animal ran  across his vehicle ahead of him he  described a creature that was between  three to four feet tall and between 50  to 75 pounds he said it was crouched  like a frog and eventually stood up on  two feet to climb over the guard rail  and head back down the river two weeks  later officer mark matthews reported  seeing the same unidentified animal  along the same roadside matthews pulled  out his rifle and shot the animal dead  upon examining the corpse he identified  it as a large iguana with a missing tail  which is why both men struggled to  identify it in the first place  stories surrounding the loveland frog  are extremely weird even for a cryptid  we are going back to west virginia and  the town of flatwoods in braxton county  for our last cryptid  the flatwoods monster also known as the  braxton county monster  this cryptid is said to be ten feet tall  and four feet wide it has a red face a  pointed hood and a dark metallic body it  was first seen in 1952  by three young boys who witnessed a  bright object fly across the sky and  crash on the land of a local farmer they  told a woman named kathleen may what  they had seen she and three of the local  boys traveled to the farm to see if the  story was true they came to the top of  the hill where the boys said the object  had landed and ahead of them was a  pulsating red light  when they pointed their flashlights in  its direction they saw a tall man with a  round face and a pointed hood  kathleen describes the monster as having  small claw-like hands a pointed hood and  a head that resembles the ace of spades  one of the boys said its eyes emitted a  green light and had a dark green body  after a few seconds the creature began  to move it made a hissing sound as it  glided towards them  as it got closer all of them recall a  pungent smell  a thick mist that burnt their eyes and  nose  they all panicked and ran away before  they could see the creature up close  the sheriff and his deputy had been  investigating reports of an aircraft  that had crashed but when they visited  the area the morning after they couldn't  see or smell anything  there were several investigations  carried out and what happened that night  has been explained in numerous ways  the bright light across the sky was most  likely a meteor  the pulsating red light could have been  an aircraft hazard beacon  and the creature with glowing eyes and  small claws could have just been an owl  this still hasn't stopped people from  claiming they've seen the flatwoods  monster as well as experiencing the  burning smell for themselves  if you've enjoyed this video and you'd  like to see more stories of cryptids  from north america and the rest of the  world then let me know in the comment  section  as we mentioned earlier today's video  has been sponsored by one dream you may  have heard me talk about the great  courses plus before while they've now  teamed up to create one dream an even  bigger better and immersive educational  experience  one dream aims to answer questions you  never even knew needed asking they have  all the same great courses plus content  but with even more of a selection to  choose from now  along with courses and lectures there  are long and short form videos tutorials  how to's and travelogues as well as a  host of interesting and engaging  documentaries  with halloween rapidly approaching i  found myself watching the three-part  series monsters within which covers the  psychology behind why horror movies are  so popular it also takes a look at  victorian horror novels such as dorian  gray and dr jekyll and their influence  on the genre  it's a great watch for anyone who enjoys  horror  if you'd like to try one dream for  yourself then visit  onedream.com  mythology to start your free trial today  [Music]  you
 

